{"tool_name":"ordo","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ordo","home":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/ordo","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"The Orphanet Rare Disease Ontology (ORDO) - structured vocabulary for rare diseases, capturing relationships between diseases, genes and other relevant features. It integrates a classification of rare diseases, relationships (gene-disease relations, epiemological data) and connections with other terminologies (MeSH, UMLS, MedDRA), databases (OMIM, UniProtKB, HGNC, ensembl, Reactome, IUPHAR, Geantlas) and classifications (ICD10).","addition_date":"2015-02-04T09:02:51Z","last_update_date":"2020-09-16T07:06:49Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Ontology","Web application"],"version":["3.0"],"collections":["RD-connect","Rare Disease"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:ordo","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ols-submission@ebi.ac.uk","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Inserm US14","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Contact Form","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/support/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/docs/index"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-EE","chandru.j"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Orpha number","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2800"}}],"note":"Data retrieval from ORDO via OLS (EMBL-EBI, UK) Identifier for records of Orphanet Rare Disease Ontology, following the regular expression: ^Orphanet(_|:)C?\\d+$.","operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Ontology concept data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0967"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"ORDO","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"CRodwell","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw170","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 The Author 2016. Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: Probability distributions play a central role in mathematical and statistical modelling. The encoding, annotation and exchange of such models could be greatly simplified by a resource providing a common reference for the definition of probability distributions. Although some resources exist, no suitably detailed and complex ontology exists nor any database allowing programmatic access. Results: ProbOnto, is an ontology-based knowledge base of probability distributions, featuring more than 80 uni- and multivariate distributions with their defining functions, characteristics, relationships and re-parameterization formulas. It can be used for model annotation and facilitates the encoding of distribution-based models, related functions and quantities. Availability and Implementation: http://probonto.org","authors":[{"name":"Grenon P."},{"name":"Swat M.J."},{"name":"Wimalaratne S."}],"citationCount":9,"date":"2016-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"ProbOnto: Ontology and knowledge base of probability distributions"},"type":["Other"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Computational biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3307"},{"term":"Data quality management","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3572"},{"term":"Ontology and terminology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0089"},{"term":"Pathology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0634"},{"term":"Rare diseases","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3325"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ORDO","home":"https://bio.tools/ordo","license":"Apache-2.0","version":"3.0","summary":"The Orphanet Rare Disease Ontology (ORDO) - structured vocabulary for rare diseases, capturing relationships between diseases, genes and other relevant features. It integrates a classification of rare diseases, relationships (ge